Syntax of Javascript

1. Variables

Variables are used to store data. In JavaScript, you declare variables using `var`, `let`, or `const`.

2. Data types

let number = 42;             // number
let string = "priya"         // string
let isactive = false         // boolean
let number = [1,2,3]         // array

3. Operators

let sum = 10 + 5;          // Arithmetic operator
let isEqual = (10 === 10); // Comparison operator
let isTrue = (true && false); // Logical operator

4. Functions
function have one name and () arguments, u can write 1,2 arguments according to u, then {right your logical}

// Function declaration
function greet(name) {
    return "Hello , " + name;
}

// Function call
let message = greet("john");  // "Hello, John"


5. If/Else

if (age >= 18) {
    console.log("You are an adult.");
} else {
    console.log("You are a minor.");
}

6. Loops

// For loop
for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    console.log(i); // Outputs 0 to 4
}

// While loop
let j = 0;
while (j < 5) {
    console.log(j); // Outputs 0 to 4
    j++;
}

